Hum's source code has no third-party dependencies. A parent can search two free symbol libraries
online; a symbol they choose is saved into their own tile. Those symbols keep their own licences.
The starter board (examples/starter/ and hum-aac-ios/Resources/starter.hum) includes 24 ARASAAC
pictograms under the ARASAAC licence below; nothing else in Hum includes symbols.

- ARASAAC pictograms by Sergio Palao. Origin: ARASAAC (https://arasaac.org). Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
  Owner: Government of Aragón (Spain). Non-commercial: a paid or commercial fork of Hum must remove
  the ARASAAC search.
- Mulberry Symbols by Steve Lee (https://mulberrysymbols.org), via Global Symbols
  (https://globalsymbols.com). Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0.

The starter board's phrases come from the open Gestalt phrases list
(https://github.com/DPWonder/gestalt-phrases) by ReadySetSay. Licence: CC BY 4.0.

